Hyperboloid of one sheet defined by x squared over 4 minus y squared over 16 plus z squared over 4 equals 1, with axis of symmetry along the y-axis. The surface has a circular waist of radius 2 at y equals 0 (shown in amber), with the cross-sections growing as the absolute value of y increases. Circular traces at y equals plus or minus 4 (radius 2 times the square root of 2) are shown in red and green. A purple hyperbola in the xz-plane shows the trace z equals 0. Intercepts at (plus or minus 2, 0, 0) and (0, 0, plus or minus 2) are marked.